---
// BaseLayout.astro — the single page shell for every migrated page.
//
// MIGRATION POSTURE (runbook Part 1, "migration not redesign"):
// Investigation of the legacy site showed the header and footer are NOT
// actually uniform — they have diverged across pages:
//   - most pages use the standard .navbar header + standard footer
//   - best-restaurants-*.html uses a different footer (different links,
//     a different phone number, different copyright) and different nav IDs
// Swapping in one canonical header/footer would therefore CHANGE visible
// content and links on those pages — a redesign, not a migration. So this
// layout deliberately does NOT impose a shared Header/Footer. Each page
// keeps its own nav and footer inline, byte-for-byte. Centralizing them
// into one component is a later, deliberate cleanup step — not migration.
//
// Each page also passes its original <head> through the `head` slot
// verbatim (title, meta, canonical, OG/Twitter, page-specific JSON-LD,
// and its own CSS link incl. the per-page ?v= cache-buster), guaranteeing
// zero metadata/schema drift.
//
// What IS centralized here (the genuinely identical scaffolding):
//   - the <html>/<head>/<body> structure and closing tags
//   - the Vimeo player script present on every page
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <slot name="head" />
</head>
<slot name="body" />
</html>
